# ROCKET_PLAN - AICS rockets: planner, tablet, flight, landing
Draft - going over with Luke. Nothing here is approved yet.

## RULES (read every pass)
- FIRST every pass: read NOTES.md + CHEATSHEET.md. Search for names, read ~100 lines around them. Never read whole big files (AicsMfd.cs, AicsMenu.cs, FlightMissions.cs, LearnFlight.cs).
- Do ONLY the first unchecked [ ] task that is not [BIG - Grok/Cursor]. Then STOP.
- Pure math goes in new static classes with no KSP types, plus a harness group in tests\csharp (Program.cs runner). Build KSPChatMod Release + tests, 0 errors.
- Log decisions with ChatLog.Write(kind, text). Chat lines with ChatWindow.Notice(...); crew lines with IntercomTalk.Fmt(name, trait, text) then Notice.
- Tools: add a case in NativeFlightController.Execute + name in NativeCommands.Ported. UI calls ChatWindow.ToolFromMenu(name, json).
- When done: mark [x], add one "done:" line (files, what, risks). Add one line to NOTES.md for new files.

## 0. Principles
- MechJeb is GPL: read it for ideas only. Never copy code, names of internals, or constants tables. Existing MechJebLink/NativeMechJebOps stay as an optional path.
- No separate rocket Learn step. Read live data (thrust, mass, Isp, drag, density) every tick and adapt as it flies.
- Plan at about the middle of what the craft can do (e.g. TWR, turn rate, throttle) to keep margin both ways.
- Every decision gets one ChatLog line with the reason (staging, throttle, abort, burn start).
- Chat/crew status is plain English, one line: "Stage 2 empty, staging." / "We are 300 m/s short for Mun landing."

## 1. Screen split (Luke's rule) - decide with Luke
Cockpit screen (AicsMenu.DrawMfdWindow / AicsIvaMfd / MfdNav groups) = only what matters for flying now: map, chart/ILS, live flight info.
Tablet = planning + tests. Map/charts may show on both. Full screen overhaul stays flexible.
- [ ] S1: List every MfdNav group/item in a table here (id, label, cockpit or tablet?). Read-only; no code. Luke decides each row.
- [ ] S2: Decide with Luke: final cockpit page list. Write it under this task.
- [ ] S3: Add a flag per MfdNav.Item "Tablet" (bool, default false). No behaviour change yet.
- [ ] S4: Hide items with Tablet=true from the cockpit MFD and AicsIvaMfd page lists (after T1 exists).
- [x] S5: Move "learn" page (NativeFlightController.LearnLines, MfdNav "learn" buttons) to the tablet Tests tab; keep START LEARN/TOGGLE/SKIP buttons working.
- [ ] S6: Tests tab per-test card: name, what it measures, status, result numbers. Data from NativeLearn.LearnLines; add a small struct if needed.
- [ ] S7: Tests tab: small graph per test (reuse T10 line graph) where the test has samples (decel, climb, stall).
- [ ] S8 [BIG - Grok/Cursor]: Full cockpit vs tablet overhaul once Luke finalises S2.

## 2. Foundation: data readers (no UI)
- [ ] D1: New StageReader.cs: read stock VesselDeltaV (vessel.VesselDeltaV.OperatingStageInfo). Per stage: dv vac/asl/actual, TWR vac/asl, burn time, start/end mass, fuel mass, Isp vac/asl. Return plain StageInfo list (no KSP types out).
- [ ] D2: StageReader: handle VesselDeltaV not ready (null / IsReady false) -> empty list + one log line, retry next second.
- [ ] D3: StageReader in editor (EditorLogic ship) so the planner works in VAB/SPH.
- [ ] D4: New LiveRocket.cs snapshot each tick: alt, radar alt, vertical/horizontal speed, q (kPa), static pressure, density, available thrust, mass, local g, max temp ratio, current stage, angular rate.
- [ ] D5: LiveRocket: available thrust and fuel flow from active engines only (respect thrust limiter, flameout).
- [ ] D6: BodyInfo helper: gravParameter, radius, atmosphere depth, SOI, rotation period, parent; for any CelestialBody by name.

## 3. Foundation: pure math + tests
- [ ] M1: RocketMath.Hohmann(mu, r1, r2) -> dv1, dv2, transfer time. Tests: LKO->Mun known numbers.
- [ ] M2: RocketMath.Circularize(mu, r, apo, peri) dv. Tests.
- [ ] M3: RocketMath.PhaseAngle(mu, r1, r2) target phase for same-SOI transfer. Tests.
- [ ] M4: RocketMath.EjectionAngle + ejection dv for interplanetary (patched conics, hyperbolic excess). Tests Kerbin->Duna.
- [ ] M5: RocketMath.CaptureDv(mu, rPeri, vInf, targetApo). Tests.
- [ ] M6: RocketMath.BurnTime(dv, mass, thrust, isp) via rocket equation, across stages. Tests.
- [ ] M7: LegBudget: needs per leg (launch, circularize, transfer, capture, land, return). Launch dv rough estimate from body (orbit speed + gravity/drag loss guess). Tests.
- [ ] M8: StageAllocator: assign legs to stages from StageInfo list; returns spare/short per leg and which stage burns it. Tests incl. leg split across 2 stages.
- [ ] M9: WindowFinder: next time phase angle matches (same SOI and around Sun). Tests.
- [ ] M10 [BIG - Grok/Cursor]: Porkchop grid (Lambert solver, departure x travel time -> dv). Tests vs known Kerbin-Duna window.
- [ ] M11: SuicideBurn.StartAlt(vs, g, thrust, mass, margin) -> altitude to start burn. Tests.
- [ ] M12: AscentProfile.TurnStart(twr) and pitch-vs-alt curve chosen from live TWR (mid-capability). Tests.
- [ ] M13: StagingPolicy.ShouldStage(flameout, tank empty, timeSince) with 0.5 s delay + reason string. Tests.
- [ ] M14: FairingPolicy.CanDeploy(q, alt, heatRatio): q<1 kPa or alt>40 km, and low heat. Tests.
- [ ] M15: AbortPolicy.Check(angRate, attErr, thrustDrop) -> reason or null. Tests for tumble + thrust loss.

